output:  JMON.s19
0001                         ; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0002                         ; JMON (Jan. 2026)
0003                         ; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0004                         ;
0005                         ; Created by GlassTTY, Jan. 2026, using MINIMON (ACH, Dec. 1978) as a base
0006                         ; with additional code from Motorola's MIKBUG.
0007                         ;
0008                         ; Special thanks to Chris Carter for inspiration and help.
0009                         ;
0010                         ; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0011                         ;
0012                         ; This is a MINIMON compatible monitor for the 77-68 Bear/Newbear system with
0013                         ; the LOAD and PUNCH commands replaced for versions that support the
0014                         ; Motorola S Record Format (.s19) files.
0015                         ;
0016                         ; All entry points and source code labels as published in the MINIMON
0017                         ; documentation have been preserved with the exception of the LOAD and PUNCH
0018                         ; commands.
0019                         ;
0020                         ; In order to make space for the additional code required, the ALTER and
0021                         ; OFFSET CALCULATION commands have been removed. This has been justified as
0022                         ; the MODIFY command has very similar functionality to ALTER making ALTER
0023                         ; unnecessary, and the OFFSET CALCULATION routines (commands X and Y) are
0024                         ; rarely used as all cross-assemblers perform these calculations
0025                         ; automatically. In addition BLOCKMOVE command (Cmd 'B') has been removed
0026                         ; to allow for a memory test command to be added (Cmd 'T')'.
0027                         ;
0028                         ; One other minor change is that the terminal along with any devices sending
0029                         ; S19 format files have been configured for 8 Data Bits, No Parity, 2 Stop
0030                         ; Bits.
0031                         ;
0032                         
0033                         
0034                         ; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0035                         ; TODO
0036                         ; One subtle code issue worth noting — in STERMR, the LDX #8 is hardcoded. The
0037                         ; comment says "A will contain the number of bytes to follow" but it ignores A
0038                         ; entirely. If whatever is sending the S19 file adds trailing whitespace or a
0039                         ; newline after S9030000FC, STERMR will consume garbage. Not related to 07D0
0040                         ; but worth knowing.
0041                         ;
0042                         ; A slight red flag in the source — FOUND in the command dispatcher does:
0043                         ;
0044                         ;   LDAB 1,X   ; B = high byte
0045                         ;   LDAA 2,X   ; A = low byte
0046                         ;   PSHA       ; pushes LOW byte first
0047                         ;   PSHB       ; pushes HIGH byte second (now on top of stack)
0048                         ;   RTS        ; 6800 RTS pulls PCH then PCL
0049                         ;
0050                         ;This actually works correctly on the 6800 — RTS pulls the top byte as PCH
0051                         ; (high) and the next as PCL (low). The inline comment in the source saying
0052                         ; "push high first" is misleading but the code is right.
0053                         ; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0054                         
0055 f401                    CTRLA   EQU     $F401       ; ACIA.A Ctrl/Status
0056 f403                    CTRLB   EQU     $F403       ; ACIA.B Ctrl/Status
0057 f400                    DATAA   EQU     $F400       ; ACIA.A Data register
0058 f402                    DATAB   EQU     $F402       ; ACIA.B Data register
0059                         
0060                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0061                         ; Note:The original 256 bytes of RAM on the CPU board
0062                         ;  appears at $F000 to $F0FE, with Switches/LEDs at $F0FF
0063                         ;  when a MON1 board is installed
0064                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0065 f0dd                    JNMI    EQU     $F0DD       ; 3 bytes for jump to NMI sub.
0066 f0e0                    JIRQ    EQU     $F0E0       ; 3 bytes for jump to IRQ sub.
0067 f0d0                    STACK   EQU     $F0D0       ; Stack goes down from $F0D0
0068                                                     ; The bytes above STACK, in
0069                                                     ; particular STACK+7 and
0070                                                     ; STACK+6 are used when the RTI
0071                                                     ; instruction is issued as part
0072                                                     ; of the GO command. Everything
0073                                                     ; from $F0D8 to $F0DC is unused
0074                                                     ; RAM.
0075                         
0076                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0077 f0d8                            ORG     $F0D8
0078                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0079                         
0080 f0d8                    T_TW    RMB     2           ; New additions to support SRec
0081 f0da                    T_CSUM  RMB     1           ;            "
0082 f0db                    T_COUNT RMB     1           ;            "
0083 f0dc                    T_TEMP  RMB     1           ;            "
0084                         
0085                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0086 f0e3                            ORG     $F0E3       ; Start of RAM variables
0087                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0088                         
0089 f0e3                    T_SAVE  RMB     2           ; Temp storage for NEWLINE
0090 f0e5                    T_P     RMB     1           ;   "     "     "  Z,X
0091 f0e6                    T_X     RMB     2           ;   "     "     "  Sub
0092 f0e8                    T_Y     RMB     2           ;   "     "     "  Sub
0093 f0ea                    T_NEW   RMB     2           ;   "     "     "  Block move
0094 f0ec                    T_M     RMB     1           ;   "     "     "  ZOUT
0095 f0ed                    T_TMPX  RMB     2           ;   "     "     "  PRX
0096 f0ef                    T_STRT  RMB     2           ;   "     "     "  GETADDRESS
0097 f0f1                    T_STOP  RMB     2           ;   "     "     "  GETADDRESS
0098 f0f3                    T_Z     RMB     2           ;   "     "     "   . RDX
0099 f0f5                    T_R     RMB     1           ;   "     "     "     PR
0100 f0f6                    T_Q     RMB     1           ;   "     "     "  ZIN,DUMP
0101 f0f7                    T_ABYT  RMB     2           ;   "     "     "  SET BR.PT.
0102 f0f9                            RMB     2           ;   "     "     "  SET BR.PT.
0103 f0fb                    T_BYTE  RMB     2           ;   "     "     "  SET BR.PT.
0104 f0fd                    PSTACK  RMB     2           ;   "     "     "     SWI etc
0105                         
0106                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0107 fc00                            ORG     $FC00       ; Start of ROM based code
0108                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0109                         
0110                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0111                         ; Read Character from ACIA
0112                         ; FC00
0113                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0114 fc00 bd fd 2b           RD_CMD  JSR     RD_A        ; Input one character
0115 fc03 27 fb                      BEQ     RD_CMD      ; Ignore paper tape follower
0116 fc05 8d 08                      BSR     PR_A        ; Echo character
0117 fc07 81 2e                      CMPA    #'.         ; Was it a fullstop ?
0118 fc09 26 11                      BNE     PRA_END ;
0119 fc0b 7e ff 8f                   JMP     START       ; Yes: Go to start of MINIMON
0120                         
0121 fc0e 01                         NOP
0122                         
0123                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0124                         ; Print character in A
0125                         ; FC0F
0126                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0127 fc0f f6 f4 01           PR_A    LDAB    CTRLA       ; Get ACIA(a) status byte
0128 fc12 c5 02                      BITB    #02         ; Is it busy ?
0129 fc14 27 f9                      BEQ     PR_A        ; Yes: Try again
0130 fc16 b7 f4 00                   STAA    DATAA       ;  No: Send data
0131 fc19 7c f0 f5                   INC     T_R         ; Characters printed + One
0132 fc1c 39                 PRA_END RTS                 ; RETURN
0133                         
0134                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0135                         ; Check A contains a HEX character,  Set C.bit on fail
0136                         ; FC1D
0137                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0138 fc1d 81 2f              VHEX    CMPA    #$2F        ; A < 30 ?
0139 fc1f 2f 0e                      BLE     NotHex      ;  not hex
0140 fc21 81 39                      CMPA    #$39        ; A > 39 ?
0141 fc23 22 02                      BHI     NotNum      ;  Not a Numeral
0142 fc25 0c                 IsHex   CLC                 ; It's OK (clear C bit)
0143 fc26 39                         RTS                 ; RETURN
0144 fc27 81 40              NotNum  CMPA    #$40        ; A < 41 ?
0145 fc29 2f 04                      BLE     NotHex      ;  not hex
0146 fc2b 81 46                      CMPA    #$46        ; A <= 46
0147 fc2d 2f f6                      BLE     IsHex       ;  then it is hex
0148 fc2f 0d                 NotHex  SEC                 ; Set C bit
0149 fc30 39                         RTS                 ; RETURN
0150                         
0151                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0152                         ; Convert A:B to binary
0153                         ; FC31
0154                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0155 fc31 85 30              BINARY  BITA    #$30        ; Is it a letter ?
0156 fc33 27 0c                      BEQ     LETTA       ; Yes: Got to handle it
0157 fc35 48                 RIDA    ASLA                ;  No: It is a number, so
0158 fc36 48                         ASLA                ;      shift
0159 fc37 48                         ASLA                ;       left
0160 fc38 48                         ASLA                ;        4 bits
0161 fc39 c5 30                      BITB    #$30        ; Is Acc.B a letter ?
0162 fc3b 27 08                      BEQ     LETTB       ; Yes: Go handle it
0163 fc3d c4 0f              RIDB    ANDB    #$0F        ; Clear 4 high bits in Acc.B
0164 fc3f 1b                         ABA                 ; Form binary character (A=A+B)
0165 fc40 39                         RTS                 ; RETURN
0166 fc41 8b 09              LETTA   ADDA    #$09        ; Make Acc.A a binary
0167 fc43 20 f0                      BRA     RIDA        ;  as before
0168 fc45 cb 09              LETTB   ADDB    #$09        ; Make Acc.B a binary
0169 fc47 20 f4                      BRA     RIDB        ;  as before
0170                         
0171                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0172                         ; Read a 4 digit HEX value, put result into X
0173                         ; FC49
0174                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0175 fc49 8d b5              ZIN     BSR     RD_CMD      ; Read a character
0176 fc4b 8d d0                      BSR     VHEX        ; Is it a hex character ?
0177 fc4d 25 10                      BCS     Z_PRQM      ; No: go to print `?`
0178 fc4f b7 f0 f6                   STAA    T_Q         ; Save it
0179 fc52 8d ac                      BSR     RD_CMD      ; Read 2nd character
0180 fc54 8d c7                      BSR     VHEX        ; Is it a hex character ?
0181 fc56 25 07                      BCS     Z_PRQM      ; No: go to print `?`
0182 fc58 16                         TAB                 ; Yes: Put it into B
0183 fc59 b6 f0 f6                   LDAA    T_Q         ; Retrieve 1st hex char to A
0184 fc5c 7e fc d8                   JMP     ZIN2        ; S19 version of ZIN is longer
0185 fc5f bd fd 21           Z_PRQM  JSR     PR_QM       ; Print "?"
0186 fc62 7e fc 49                   JMP     ZIN         ; Go back to start of hex input
0187                         
0188                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0189                         ; Read 4 hex digits and put value into X
0190                         ; FC65
0191                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0192 fc65 bd fd 4d           RD_X    JSR     PRSP        ; Print a space
0193 fc68 8d df                      BSR     ZIN         ; Read 2 digit hex value into A
0194 fc6a b7 f0 f3                   STAA    T_Z         ; Save byte (most significant)
0195 fc6d 8d da                      BSR     ZIN         ; Read 2 digit hex value into A
0196 fc6f b7 f0 f4                   STAA    T_Z+1       ; Save byte (least significant)
0197 fc72 fe f0 f3                   LDX     T_Z         ; Load full 4 hex value into X
0198 fc75 39                         RTS                 ; RETURN
0199                         
0200                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0201                         ; Print string FOLLOWING JSR ( terminated by $FF )
0202                         ;  IE: It starts at the `return addr` put onto the stack by JSR
0203                         ;  So actual return address needed is past the string
0204                         ; FC76
0205                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0206 fc76 30                 STRING  TSX                 ; Get loc. of return addr to X
0207 fc77 ee 00                      LDX     0,X         ; Get return addr to X
0208 fc79 09                         DEX                 ; Point to byte before
0209 fc7a 08                 AGAIN   INX                 ; Point to next byte
0210 fc7b a6 00                      LDAA    0,X         ; Get byte to be printed
0211 fc7d 81 ff                      CMPA    #$FF        ; End-string ?
0212 fc7f 27 04                      BEQ     ENDSTR      ; Yes: Go to finish up
0213 fc81 8d 8c                      BSR     PR_A        ; Print the byte
0214 fc83 20 f5                      BRA     AGAIN       ; Go back for next byte
0215 fc85 31                 ENDSTR  INS                 ; Clean up stack...
0216 fc86 31                         INS                 ;  ( pop off the return addr )
0217 fc87 6e 01                      JMP     1,X         ; Jump back to caller (RETURN)
0218                         
0219                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0220                         ; FC89
0221                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0222 fc89 8d eb              GETADD  BSR     STRING      ; Print string...
0223 fc8b 20 53                      FCC     " S"
0224 fc8d ff                         FCB     $FF         ; End-of-string
0225 fc8e 8d d5                      BSR     RD_X        ; Read 4 digit HEX addr value
0226 fc90 ff f0 ef                   STX     T_STRT      ; Save it
0227 fc93 8d e1                      BSR     STRING      ; Print string...
0228 fc95 20 46                      FCC     " F"
0229 fc97 ff                         FCB     $FF         ; End-of-string
0230 fc98 8d cb                      BSR     RD_X        ; Read 4 digit HEX addr value
0231 fc9a ff f0 f1                   STX     T_STOP      ; Save it
0232 fc9d 39                         RTS                 ; RETURN
0233                         
0234                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0235                         ; Convert value in A to 2 x ASCII hex digits in A and B
0236                         ; FC9E
0237                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0238 fc9e 16                 ASCII   TAB                 ; Copy A to B
0239 fc9f 84 f0                      ANDA    #$F0        ; Clear low order 4 bits of A
0240 fca1 44                         LSRA                ; Shift
0241 fca2 44                         LSRA                ;  right
0242 fca3 44                         LSRA                ;   4
0243 fca4 44                         LSRA                ;    bits
0244 fca5 81 09                      CMPA    #$09        ; Letter or number ?
0245 fca7 22 0b                      BHI     SUBT        ;
0246 fca9 8b 30                      ADDA    #$30        ; Make it an ASCII number
0247 fcab c4 0f              AND     ANDB    #$0F        ; Clear high order bits of B
0248 fcad c1 09                      CMPB    #$09        ; Letter or number ?
0249 fcaf 22 07                      BHI     ADD
0250 fcb1 cb 30                      ADDB    #$30        ; Make it an ASCII number
0251 fcb3 39                         RTS                 ; RETURN
0252 fcb4 8b 37              SUBT    ADDA    #$37        ; Make it an ASCI letter
0253 fcb6 20 f3                      BRA     AND         ; Go to process low order value
0254 fcb8 cb 37              ADD     ADDB    #$37        ; Make it an ASII letter
0255 fcba 39                         RTS                 ; RETURN
0256                         
0257                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0258                         ; Print value in X as 4 hex digits
0259                         ; FCBB
0260                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0261 fcbb ff f0 ed           PRX     STX     T_TMPX      ; Save X
0262 fcbe b6 f0 ed                   LDAA    T_TMPX      ; Get high order byte to A
0263 fcc1 8d 06                      BSR     ZOUT        ; Print A as 2 hex digits
0264 fcc3 b6 f0 ee                   LDAA    T_TMPX+1    ; Get low order byte to A
0265 fcc6 20 01                      BRA     ZOUT        ; Print A as 2 hex digits
0266                         
0267 fcc8 01                         NOP
0268                         
0269                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0270                         ; Print value in A as 2 hex digits, Preserve B
0271                         ; X unchanged by called routines
0272                         ; FCC9
0273                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0274 fcc9 37                 ZOUT    PSHB                ; Save B to STACK
0275 fcca 36                         PSHA                ; Save A to STACK
0276 fccb 8d d1                      BSR     ASCII       ; Convert A to ASCII in A & B
0277 fccd 37                         PSHB                ; Save B (2nd byte) to STACK
0278 fcce bd fc 0f                   JSR     PR_A        ; Print byte in A
0279 fcd1 32                         PULA                ; Get 2nd byte into A from STACK
0280 fcd2 bd fc 0f                   JSR     PR_A        ; Print byte in A
0281 fcd5 32                         PULA                ; Recover A from STACK
0282 fcd6 33                         PULB                ; Recover B from STACK
0283 fcd7 39                         RTS                 ; RETURN
0284                         
0285                         ; second part of S19 version of ZIN
0286 fcd8 bd fc 31           ZIN2    JSR     BINARY      ; Convert A:B to binary to A
0287 fcdb 16                         TAB                 ; B=A
0288 fcdc fb f0 da                   ADDB    T_CSUM      ; Add this value
0289 fcdf f7 f0 da                   STAB    T_CSUM      ; to the Checksum (for S19)
0290 fce2 39                         RTS                 ; RETURN
0291                         
0292                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0293                         ; S19 format data load : Modded version of Mikbug code
0294                         ; FCE3
0295                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0296 fce3                    LOAD    EQU     *           ; L = Load = Input an S19 file
0297 fce3 8d 91                      BSR     STRING
0298 fce5 0d 0a                      FCB     $0D,$0A     ; c/r l/f
0299 fce7 ff                         FCB     $FF         ; End-Of-String
0300 fce8 bd fc 00           LREAD   JSR     RD_CMD      ; Read+Echo, test for '.'
0301 fceb 81 53                      CMPA    #'S         ; Is it `S` ?
0302 fced 26 f9                      BNE     LREAD       ; No: Keep waiting for `S`
0303 fcef bd fc 00                   JSR     RD_CMD      ; Read+Echo, test for '.'
0304 fcf2 81 39                      CMPA    #'9         ; Is it `9` ?  ( `S9` record )
0305 fcf4 26 03                      BNE     LREAD1
0306 fcf6 7e fe b3                   JMP     STERMR      ; handle termination record
0307 fcf9 81 31              LREAD1  CMPA    #'1         ; Is it `1` ?  ( `S1` record )
0308 fcfb 26 eb                      BNE     LREAD       ; No: Wait for next `S`
0309 fcfd 7f f0 da                   CLR     T_CSUM      ; Clear checksum
0310 fd00 bd fc 49                   JSR     ZIN         ; Read 2xHex = data.byte count to A
0311 fd03 80 02                      SUBA    #2          ; Subtract 2 (to get bytes left in line)
0312 fd05 b7 f0 db                   STAA    T_COUNT     ; Store byte count
0313 fd08 bd fc 65                   JSR     RD_X        ; Read 4xHex digit address to X
0314 fd0b bd fc 49           LDOBYT  JSR     ZIN         ; Read 2xHex digits, value to A
0315 fd0e 7a f0 db                   DEC     T_COUNT     ; Decrement our byte count
0316 fd11 27 05                      BEQ     LCHK        ; If end-of-line, go look at checksum
0317 fd13 a7 00                      STAA    0,X         ; Save byte where X points
0318 fd15 08                         INX                 ; Point X at next byte
0319 fd16 20 f3                      BRA     LDOBYT      ; Go get next byte
0320 fd18 7c f0 da           LCHK    INC     T_CSUM      ; Add 1 to checksum
0321 fd1b 27 cb                      BEQ     LREAD       ; OK: Go read next record
0322 fd1d 8d 02                      BSR     PR_QM       ; Print "?"
0323 fd1f 20 29                      BRA     STARTR      ; Go to START
0324                         
0325 fd21 86 3f              PR_QM   LDAA #'?            ; Put '?' character in A
0326 fd23 7e fc 0f                   JMP     PR_A        ; Print it and return via PR_As RTS
0327                         
0328 fd26 01                         NOP
0329 fd27 01                         NOP
0330 fd28 01                         NOP
0331 fd29 01                         NOP
0332 fd2a 01                         NOP
0333                         
0334                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0335                         ; Read byte from ACIA.A to A
0336                         ; FD2B
0337                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0338 fd2b b6 f4 01           RD_A    LDAA    CTRLA       ; Get ACIA.A status byte
0339 fd2e 85 01                      BITA    #$01        ; Is byte ready in DATAA
0340 fd30 27 f9                      BEQ     RD_A        ; No: Try again
0341 fd32 7e fd d0                   JMP     PARITY      ; Need to clear parity as we
0342                                                     ; need to support 7E2 & 8N2
0343                         
0344 fd35 01                         NOP
0345                         
0346                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0347                         ; FD36
0348                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0349 fd36 8d 15              REGPRT  BSR     PRSP        ; Print a space
0350 fd38 fe f0 fd                   LDX     PSTACK      ; Point X at user's stack
0351 fd3b 8d 1c                      BSR     PR2         ; Print CC
0352 fd3d 8d 1a                      BSR     PR2         ; Print B
0353 fd3f 8d 18                      BSR     PR2         ; Print A
0354 fd41 8d 10                      BSR     PR4         ; Print X
0355 fd43 8d 0e                      BSR     PR4         ; Print PC
0356 fd45 ce f0 fd                   LDX     #PSTACK     ; Point X at stack pointer
0357 fd48 8d 0a                      BSR     PR4X        ; Print stack pointer
0358 fd4a 7e ff 8f           STARTR  JMP     START       ; (RETURN) to MINIMON
0359                         
0360                         
0361                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0362                         ; FD4D
0363                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0364 fd4d 86 20              PRSP    LDAA    #$20        ; Put space character in A
0365 fd4f bd fc 0f                   JSR     PR_A        ; Print it
0366 fd52 39                         RTS                 ; RETURN
0367                         
0368 fd53 08                 PR4     INX                 ; Point X to next character
0369 fd54 a6 00              PR4X    LDAA    0,X         ; Get byte pointed to by X
0370 fd56 bd fc c9                   JSR     ZOUT        ; Print it
0371 fd59 08                 PR2     INX                 ; Point X to next character
0372 fd5a a6 00                      LDAA    0,X         ; Get byte pointed to by X
0373 fd5c bd fc c9                   JSR     ZOUT        ; Print it
0374 fd5f 8d ec                      BSR     PRSP        ; Print a space
0375 fd61 39                         RTS                 ; RETURN
0376                         
0377                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0378                         ; FD62
0379                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0380 fd62 bd fc 89           MEMTEST JSR     GETADD      ; get the start and finish addresses
0381 fd65 bd fc 76                   JSR     STRING
0382 fd68 20 54 45 53 54 49          FCC     " TESTING..."
     4e 47 2e 2e 2e
0383 fd73 ff                         FCB     $FF
0384 fd74 5f                         CLRB                ; clearing B means that we go through
0385                                                     ;  process 256 times
0386 fd75 fe f0 ef           .TST    LDX     T_STRT      ; put start address in X
0387 fd78 4f                         CLRA
0388 fd79 1b                 .LOOP1  ABA                 ; create the pattern
0389 fd7a a7 00                      STAA    0,X         ; Write to memory
0390 fd7c 08                         INX
0391 fd7d bc f0 f1                   CPX     T_STOP      ; Check for end of memory
0392 fd80 26 f7                      BNE     .LOOP1
0393 fd82 fe f0 ef                   LDX     T_STRT
0394 fd85 4f                         CLRA
0395 fd86 1b                 .LOOP2  ABA
0396 fd87 a1 00                      CMPA     0,X        ; Read from memory
0397 fd89 26 1d                      BNE     .FAULT
0398 fd8b 08                 .NOPR   INX
0399 fd8c bc f0 f1                   CPX     T_STOP
0400 fd8f 26 f5                      BNE     .LOOP2
0401 fd91 b6 f4 01                   LDAA    CTRLA       ; Read ACIA status
0402 fd94 85 01                      BITA    #$01        ; Key waiting?
0403 fd96 26 03                      BNE     .END        ; Yes so end the test
0404 fd98 5c                         INCB                ; change the pattern and repeat
0405 fd99 26 da                      BNE     .TST        ; we loop the test 256 times
0406 fd9b b6 f4 00           .END    LDAA    DATAA       ; Clear a byte from ACIA
0407 fd9e bd fc 76                   JSR     STRING
0408 fda1 20 4f 4b                   FCC     " OK"
0409 fda4 ff                         FCB     $FF
0410 fda5 7e ff 8f                   JMP     START
0411                         
0412 fda8 36                 .FAULT  PSHA                ; save current pattern
0413 fda9 a6 00                      LDAA 0,X
0414 fdab 36                         PSHA                ; save val in failed memory location
0415 fdac bd fe 97                   JSR     NEWLINE     ; print address
0416 fdaf bd fd 4d                   JSR     PRSP        ; print a space
0417 fdb2 32                         PULA                ; get val in failed memory location
0418 fdb3 bd fc c9                   JSR     ZOUT        ;  and print it
0419 fdb6 bd fc 76                   JSR     STRING      ; add some text
0420 fdb9 21 3d                      FCC     "!="
0421 fdbb ff                         FCB     $FF
0422 fdbc 32                         PULA                ; get the pattern it should be
0423 fdbd bd fc c9                   JSR     ZOUT        ;  and print it
0424 fdc0 7e ff 8f                   JMP     START       ; all done
0425                         
0426 fdc3 01                         NOP
0427                         
0428                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0429                         ; FDC4
0430                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0431 fdc4 bd fc 76           VERSION JSR     STRING
0432 fdc7 20 30 2e 30 32             FCC     " 0.02"
0433 fdcc ff                         FCB     $FF
0434 fdcd 7e ff 8f           .VEND   JMP     START
0435                         
0436 fdd0 b6 f4 00           PARITY  LDAA    DATAA       ; Get the data byte to A
0437 fdd3 84 7f                      ANDA    #$7F        ; Mask off parity bit if it exists
0438 fdd5 39                         RTS                 ; RETURN
0439                         
0440                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0441                         ; FDD6
0442                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0443 fdd6 ce f0 e6           SUB     LDX     #T_X        ; Point X to start of T_X data
0444 fdd9 a6 01                      LDAA    1,X         ; A = T_X (low)
0445 fddb e6 00                      LDAB    0,X         ; B = T_X (high)
0446 fddd a0 03                      SUBA    3,X         ; A = A - T_Y (low)
0447 fddf e2 02                      SBCB    2,X         ; B = B - T_Y (high)
0448 fde1 39                         RTS                 ; RETURN
0449                         
0450                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0451                         ; S format data output : Modded version of Mikbug code
0452                         ; FDE2
0453                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0454 fde2 bd fc 89           PUNCH   JSR     GETADD      ; Prompt for "Start:","Stop:"
0455 fde5 fe f0 ef                   LDX     T_STRT      ; Get start address
0456 fde8 ff f0 d8                   STX     T_TW        ; save it to work area
0457 fdeb b6 f0 f2           POUT1   LDAA    T_STOP+1    ; get low order of end address
0458 fdee b0 f0 d9                   SUBA    T_TW+1      ; Subtract low order start
0459 fdf1 f6 f0 f1                   LDAB    T_STOP      ; ( carry not affected by LDA )
0460 fdf4 f2 f0 d8                   SBCB    T_TW        ; Subtract with Carry
0461 fdf7 26 04                      BNE     POUT2
0462 fdf9 81 10                      CMPA    #16
0463 fdfb 25 02                      BCS     POUT3
0464 fdfd 86 0f              POUT2   LDAA    #15
0465 fdff 8b 04              POUT3   ADDA    #4
0466 fe01 b7 f0 db                   STAA    T_COUNT     ; FRAME COUNT THIS RECORD
0467 fe04 80 03                      SUBA    #3
0468 fe06 b7 f0 dc                   STAA    T_TEMP      ; BYTE COUNT THIS RECORD
0469 fe09 bd fc 76                   JSR     STRING      ; Output this string...
0470 fe0c 0d 0a                      FCB     $0D,$0A     ; c/r l/f
0471 fe0e 53 31                      FCB     'S,'1       ; S1
0472 fe10 ff                         FCB     $FF         ; End-Of-String
0473 fe11 5f                         CLRB                ; Clear checksum
0474                         
0475                         ; Output frame count...
0476 fe12 ce f0 db                   LDX     #T_COUNT    ; X = Address of Framecount
0477 fe15 bd fe a8                   JSR     POUTH2      ; O/P byte <-X and inc X
0478                         
0479                         ; Output address...
0480 fe18 ce f0 d8                   LDX     #T_TW
0481 fe1b bd fe a8                   JSR     POUTH2      ; O/P byte <-X and inc X
0482 fe1e bd fe a8                   JSR     POUTH2      ; O/P byte <-X and inc X
0483                         
0484                         ; Output data...
0485 fe21 fe f0 d8                   LDX     T_TW
0486 fe24 bd fe a8           POUT4   JSR     POUTH2      ; O/P byte <-X and inc X
0487 fe27 7a f0 dc                   DEC     T_TEMP      ; Decrement `bytes left` count
0488 fe2a 26 f8                      BNE     POUT4       ; Loop back if any left
0489 fe2c ff f0 d8                   STX     T_TW
0490 fe2f 53                         COMB
0491 fe30 37                         PSHB
0492 fe31 30                         TSX                 ; X = S + 1
0493 fe32 8d 74                      BSR     POUTH2      ; PUNCH CHECKSUM
0494 fe34 33                         PULB
0495 fe35 fe f0 d8                   LDX     T_TW
0496 fe38 09                         DEX
0497 fe39 bc f0 f1                   CPX     T_STOP
0498 fe3c 26 ad                      BNE     POUT1
0499 fe3e 7e ff dd                   JMP     STERMS
0500                         
0501 fe41 01                         NOP
0502 fe42 01                         NOP
0503                         
0504                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0505                         ; FE43
0506                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0507 fe43 bd fc 65           MODIFY  JSR     RD_X        ; Get address to X
0508 fe46 bd fd 4d           STRT    JSR     PRSP        ; Print a space
0509 fe49 7f f0 f5                   CLR     T_R         ; T_R = 0
0510 fe4c a6 00              PRz     LDAA    0,X         ; Get byte pointed to by X to A
0511 fe4e bd fc c9                   JSR     ZOUT        ; Print it as 2.hex digits
0512 fe51 bd fc 00           WATSIT  JSR     RD_CMD      ; Get command character
0513 fe54 81 20              WHAT    CMPA    #$20        ; Is it a space ?
0514 fe56 26 0c                      BNE     ISSLSH      ; No: go test for slash
0515 fe58 08                 CARYON  INX                 ; Increment X
0516 fe59 b6 f0 f5                   LDAA    T_R         ; A = T_R
0517 fe5c 81 16                      CMPA    #$16        ; At end of line ?
0518 fe5e 2f ec                      BLE     PRz         ; No: Loop back to continue
0519 fe60 8d 35              NEW_1   BSR     NEWLINE     ; Print c/r l/f nul
0520 fe62 20 e2                      BRA     STRT        ; Loop back (Note: Hex was wrong in doc, E2 instead of E5)
0521                         
0522 fe64 81 2f              ISSLSH  CMPA    #'/         ; Is it a slash ?
0523 fe66 26 03                      BNE     ISCRET      ; No: go test for c/r
0524 fe68 09                         DEX                 ; X = X - 1
0525 fe69 20 f5                      BRA     NEW_1       ; Loop back (print newline)
0526                         
0527 fe6b 81 0d              ISCRET  CMPA    #$0D        ; Is it a c/r ?
0528 fe6d 26 03                      BNE     ISHEX       ; No: go test for valid Hex
0529 fe6f 08                         INX                 ; X = X + 1
0530 fe70 20 ee                      BRA     NEW_1       ; Loop back (print newline)
0531                         
0532 fe72 bd fc 1d           ISHEX   JSR     VHEX        ; Is it a valid hex character ?
0533 fe75 25 19                      BCS     PRQM        ; No: print `?` and ignore
0534 fe77 b7 f0 f6                   STAA    T_Q         ; T_Q = A : Save it
0535 fe7a bd fc 00                   JSR     RD_CMD      ; Get 2nd character
0536 fe7d bd fc 1d                   JSR     VHEX        ; Is it a valid hex character ?
0537 fe80 25 d2                      BCS     WHAT        ; No: then see what it is
0538 fe82 16                         TAB                 ; B = A
0539 fe83 b6 f0 f6                   LDAA    T_Q         ; A = T_Q
0540 fe86 bd fc 31                   JSR     BINARY      ; Convert to binary value
0541 fe89 a7 00                      STAA    0,X         ; Store it
0542 fe8b bd fd 4d                   JSR     PRSP        ; Print a space
0543 fe8e 20 c8                      BRA     CARYON      ; Loop back
0544                         
0545 fe90 86 3f              PRQM    LDAA    #'?         ; Put `?` into A
0546 fe92 bd fc 0f                   JSR     PR_A        ; Print it
0547 fe95 20 ba                      BRA     WATSIT      ; Loop back
0548                         
0549 fe97 ff f0 e3           NEWLINE STX     T_SAVE      ; Save X
0550 fe9a bd fc 76                   JSR     STRING      ; Print string...
0551 fe9d 0d 0a 00                   FCB     $0D,$0A,$00
0552 fea0 ff                         FCB     $FF         ; End-of-string
0553 fea1 fe f0 e3                   LDX     T_SAVE      ; Restore X
0554 fea4 bd fc bb                   JSR     PRX         ; Print X
0555 fea7 39                         RTS                 ; RETURN
0556                         
0557 fea8 eb 00              POUTH2 ADDB    0,X          ; Update checksum
0558 feaa 36                         PSHA                ; Push A to STACK
0559 feab a6 00                      LDAA    0,X         ; Load byte to be o/p
0560 fead bd fc c9                   JSR     ZOUT        ; O/P byte <- X
0561 feb0 32                         PULA                ; Pull A off STACK
0562 feb1 08                         INX                 ; Increment X
0563 feb2 39                         RTS                 ; RETURN
0564                         
0565                         ; Processes the termination record which, if we get here is an S9 record
0566                         ; A will contain the umber of bytes to follow (should be 39h i.e. ASCII '9')
0567                         ; which means there are left to absorb.
0568 feb3 ce 00 08           STERMR  LDX     #8          ; get the number of bytes left in record
0569 feb6 bd fc 00           STERM1  JSR     RD_CMD      ; read and echo from ACIA and ignore
0570 feb9 09                         DEX
0571 feba 26 fa                      BNE     STERM1      ; loop for remaining bytes
0572 febc 7e ff 8f           STARTS  JMP     START
0573                         
0574 febf 01                         NOP
0575 fec0 01                         NOP
0576 fec1 01                         NOP
0577                         
0578                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0579                         ; FEC2
0580                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0581 fec2 bd fc 65           GO      JSR     RD_X        ; Get address to X (16.bit)
0582 fec5 bd fc 00                   JSR     RD_CMD      ; Right address ?
0583 fec8 b6 f0 f4                   LDAA    T_Z+1       ; T_Z.low to A
0584 fecb f6 f0 f3                   LDAB    T_Z         ; T_Z.high to B
0585 fece fe f0 fd           GOTO    LDX     PSTACK      ; Callers stack address to X
0586 fed1 a7 07                      STAA    7,X         ; Put new return
0587 fed3 e7 06                      STAB    6,X         ; address on stack
0588 fed5 be f0 fd                   LDS     PSTACK      ; Set up calling programs stack
0589 fed8 3b                         RTI                 ; RETURN-FROM-INTERRUPT (SWI)
0590                         
0591                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0592                         ; FED9
0593                         ; -----------------------------------------------------
0594 fed9 bd fc 00           CONTNU  JSR     RD_CMD      ; Read a byte (test for `.`)
0595 fedc 81 31                      CMPA    #'1         ; Is it `1` ?
0596 fede 26 10                      BNE     IsIt2       ; No: go test for `2`
0597 fee0 fe f0 f7                   LDX     T_ABYT      ; Get address of break.point
0598 fee3 b6 f0 fb                   LDAA    T_BYTE      ; Get saved opcode
0599 fee6 a7 00                      STAA    0,X         ; Put it back in the program
0600 fee8 b6 f0 f8                   LDAA    T_ABYT+1     ; Get address at which
0601 feeb f6 f0 f7                   LDAB    T_ABYT      ;   to re-enter program
0602 feee 20 de                      BRA     GOTO        ; Go to calling program
0603                         
0604 fef0 81 32              IsIt2   CMPA    #'2         ; Is it `2`
0605 fef2 27 03                      BEQ     G_Is2       ; Yes: go process it
0606 fef4 7e ff 8f                   JMP     START       ; No: Return to MINIMON
0607 fef7 fe f0 f9           G_Is2   LDX     T_ABYT+2    ; Get addr. of break.point 2
0608 fefa b6 f0 fc                   LDAA    T_BYTE+1    ; Get old opcode
0609 fefd a7 00                      STAA    0,X         ; Put it back
0610 feff b6 f0 fa                   LDAA    T_ABYT+3    ; Load address to start
0611 ff02 f6 f0 f9                   LDAB    T_ABYT+2    ;  running program at
0612 ff05 20 c7                      BRA     GOTO        ; Run user program
0613                         
